This is a project for my BA dissertation in Archaeology at the University of Leicester, analysing the positions of memorials called hero-stones in the south Indian city of Bengaluru.

Hero-stones are multi-level stone structures that were installed across India through ancient and medieval times to commemorate "heroes", individuals who died while saving their communities. My immediate goals with this code were to check if (1) the stones in Bengaluru form clusters, and (2) the stones are preferentially placed on high-visibility peaks compared to valleys. The two programs for this are Clustering_Program.py and Peak_Identification.py; Trough_Identification.py is the reverse of the peak-identifying program, for identifying hero-stones located in troughs. All these programs use the base dataset of hero-stones in this repository (a bigger version of the dataset is also listed). 

Additionally, a map-plotting program is listed as well: this needs a DEM of the Bengaluru region and a ShapeMap of the district's boundaries, which are also included in the repository.

